Z||000000||Jeff-87||07-05-2001||01:16 AM||||Hi, I just purchased a Pontiac Cassette/Radio (UP3) and have read the other posts on installing these radio (great information!).  My questions is do I need to adapt the antenna down to the new smaller plug style?  Also, does anyone have a GM part number for it, or is it a lot cheaper to get elsewhere?  Also, where is the cheapest place to get the radio adapter plug?  Thanks for the help.<BR>Jeff||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||07-05-2001||01:38 AM||||Yes, you need to adapt the antenna.....the wiring adapter for the radio comes as a kit with the antenna adapter also. The GM part number is 16140051 and list price is $18.25.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                   <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                    </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jeff-87||07-05-2001||02:08 AM||||Thanks for the info Terry.  That is exactly what I needed to know.  I am excited to get it installed.  From the picture of everyone elses, they look sweet.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Jeff||||reg||10
